{"t": 1794113399.0427077, "kind": "call", "tool": "github_push_files", "args": {"branch": "fix/pagination-57", "files": [{"content": "def page(items: list, number: int, size: int) -> list:\n    \"\"\"Return a single page of ``items``.\n\n    ``number`` is 1-based, matching the API's ``?page=1`` convention.\n    \"\"\"\n    start = (number - 1) * size\n    return items[start:start + size]\n", "path": "catalog/pager.py"}], "message": "Fix 1-based pagination in catalog.pager.page (#57)", "owner": "acme", "repo": "catalog"}, "ok": true}
{"t": 1794113402.4937449, "kind": "call", "tool": "github_create_pull_request", "args": {"base": "main", "body": "## Summary\n\n`catalog.pager.page()` treated `number` as 0-based, so `page(items, 1, size)` returned the second page. Issue #57 notes that the API documents page numbers as 1-based (`?page=1` is the first page).\n\n## Change\n\n- `catalog/pager.py`: compute the offset as `(number - 1) * size` instead of `number * size`, and document the 1-based contract in the docstring.\n\n## Verification\n\nRan local assertions against a 25-item list:\n\n- `page(items, 1, 10) == items[0:10]`\n- `page(items, 2, 10) == items[10:20]`\n- `page(items, 3, 10) == items[20:25]`\n- `page(items, 4, 10) == []`\n- `page([], 1, 5) == []`\n\nAll passed.\n\nCloses #57", "head": "fix/pagination-57", "owner": "acme", "repo": "catalog", "title": "Fix 1-based pagination in page() (#57)"}, "ok": true}
